+# Four-Week Evidence Literacy Plan
+
+## Confirmed choices
+
+- Learner: Grade 9
+- Focus: Community water quality
+- Schedule: Tuesday, Thursday, Saturday
+- Access: Offline-capable
+- Feedback: Paired peer review
+- Capstone: Three-minute recorded audio briefing
+- Total scheduled time: 460 minutes
+
+## Week 1 — Frame the Question
+
+| Day | Phase | Module | Minutes | Materials | Evidence of learning |
+|---|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| Tuesday | Launch | Notice Wonder Question | 35 | Observation photo cards | Inquiry question with three observations |
+| Thursday | Practice | Map the Water Story | 45 | Local watershed map | Cause-and-effect map with two testable links |
+| Saturday | Check | Question Quality Sort | 30 | Question quality cards | Revised focused inquiry question |
+
+## Week 2 — Evaluate Sources
+
+| Day | Phase | Module | Minutes | Materials | Evidence of learning |
+|---|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| Tuesday | Launch | Library Source Trail | 40 | Library source trail log | Three-source trail with call numbers and access dates |
+| Thursday | Practice | Claim Evidence Match Lab | 50 | Printed evidence packet | Claim-evidence matches for four excerpts |
+| Saturday | Check | Source Reliability Exit Ticket | 25 | Source reliability checklist | Reliability judgment for three sources |
+
+## Week 3 — Build the Claim
+
+| Day | Phase | Module | Minutes | Materials | Evidence of learning |
+|---|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| Tuesday | Launch | From Data to Claim | 35 | Claim frame | Draft claim supported by two data points |
+| Thursday | Practice | Counterclaim Workshop | 45 | Counterclaim cards | Response to one evidence-based counterclaim |
+| Saturday | Check | Evidence Swap Peer Review | 40 | Peer review guide | Two peer comments and one planned revision |
+
+## Week 4 — Publish and Reflect
+
+| Day | Phase | Module | Minutes | Materials | Evidence of learning |
+|---|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| Tuesday | Launch | Audio Briefing Storyboard | 35 | Audio storyboard | Timed storyboard with claim evidence and closing |
+| Thursday | Practice | Record Listen Revise | 50 | Offline voice recorder | Three-minute audio draft plus revision log |
+| Saturday | Check | Community Briefing Reflection | 30 | Reflection sheet | Final audio briefing and reflection naming one peer-led revision |
+
+## Assessment checkpoints
+
+- Question: Frame one focused question about community water quality that can be answered with evidence and is grounded in at least three observations.
+- Source judgment: Evaluate authority, currency, relevance, and corroboration across at least three sources.
+- Evidence reasoning: Support the claim with at least two data points and answer one evidence-based counterclaim.
+- Communication and reflection: Deliver a three-minute recorded audio briefing and document one revision prompted by paired peer review.
+
